  "body": "When we install matrix-synapse from the debian repository, we have the following part in the file `homeserver.yaml` (commented by default) : \r\n\r\n```yaml\r\nldap_config:\r\n   enabled: true\r\n   server: \"ldap://localhost\"\r\n   port: 389\r\n   tls: false\r\n   search_base: \"ou=Users,dc=example,dc=com\"\r\n   search_property: \"cn\"\r\n   email_property: \"email\"\r\n   full_name_property: \"givenName\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I try to launch my server with this configuration (and the correct value for each keys !), I've the following error : \r\n\r\n```\r\nLDAP enabled but missing required config values: uri, base, attributes\r\n```\r\n\r\nIndeed, lot of modifications were made, and now this configuration file is deprecated and prevent matrix-synapse from booting. I'm currently using the following configuration keys : \r\n\r\n```yaml\r\nldap_config:\r\n  enabled: true\r\n  uri: \"ldap://localhost\"\r\n  port: 389\r\n  tls: false\r\n  bind_dn: \"dn=Auth,dc=example,dc=com\"\r\n  bind_password: \"password\"\r\n  base: \"ou=Users,dc=example,dc=com\"\r\n  attributes:\r\n    uid: \"cn\"\r\n    name: \"displayName\"\r\n    mail: \"mail\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n*server became uri, search_base became base, search_property, email_property and full_name_property were renamed and placed under attributes*\r\n\r\nAnd my server if now working even if name and mail attributes are not really used yet.\r\nI don't know where and/or how `homeserver.yaml` is generated.",
